# SFR writes that legitimately appear in SOME build tiers and not others.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. audit_sfr_writes.py scans mboxfw/build/*.rst -- the
# LAST BUILD, whatever it was -- and fails on any entry in sfr_writes.allowed
# that the build does not emit. That check is worth keeping: a write that
# silently disappears is exactly how a delay loop or an endpoint arm goes
# missing. But the manifest is baselined against ONE image, and mboxfw has
# several tiers that differ by design (release / diagnostic, MBOX_SERIAL_EEPROM,
# MBOX_PROVISION). Before this file, building any tier other than the baselined
# one turned the gate red for a reason that was not a defect, and the only way
# to get it green was `--update`, which quietly re-baselines onto whatever
# happens to be in build/ -- the failure mode this gate exists to prevent.
#
# So: entries listed here are exempt from the REMOVED check only. They are
# still subject to the NEW check -- an address appearing that is in neither
# file still fails. Absence is forgiven; presence is not.
#
# --update does not write this file. Add rows by hand, with a reason.
#
# Format matches sfr_writes.allowed: ADDR  PATTERN  IMMEDIATE  # reason

# IEPDCNTX0, the EP0 IN byte count, armed by push_reply_chunk() with the
# packet length. The write is `IEPDCNTX0 = n` and exists in EVERY tier -- what
# is tier-dependent is only how SDCC codes it. With MBOX_SERIAL_EEPROM the
# function carries a second copy loop for the XDATA reply source (the EEPROM
# serial string), and the extra branch leaves a `movx a,@dptr` on the same DPTR
# ahead of the store, so the scanner reads it as rmw. Without that branch the
# same line scans as `runtime`, which is separately listed in the manifest.
# Both classifications are the same source line at src/usb.c:297.
0xff6b  rmw       -       # tier: MBOX_SERIAL_EEPROM only (codegen shape of IEPDCNTX0 = n)

# The four I2C writes that exist ONLY on the EEPROM READ path, i.e. only in
# builds carrying eeprom_read_seq() -- MBOX_SERIAL_EEPROM (#221) and
# MBOX_PROVISION (#226). A compile-time-serial build (MBOX_UNIT=A/B) or a plain
# release build has no reader and emits none of them. All four are cited to TI
# I2c.c::I2CAccess in eeprom.c and justified in rev20_diff_justifications.md.
0xffc0  or        0x02    # tier: read path only -- STOP_READ  (TI I2c.c line 136)
0xffc1  assign    0xff    # tier: read path only -- dummy write (TI I2c.c line 111)
0xffc2  rmw       -       # tier: read path only -- I2CDATI     (TI I2c.c line 140)
0xffc3  assign    0xa1    # tier: read path only -- read address (TI I2c.c line 96)
